# Vendored shared-process-kit artifacts are hashed byte-for-byte by the
# tier-1 drift test (tests/test_kit_drift.py), which splits each file at its
# END KIT PROVENANCE marker and asserts the body sha256 equals the kit
# manifest value. A checkout that rewrote CRLF<->LF would change the body
# bytes and break the hash, so these paths are pinned to LF and marked
# non-text. snap.sh sets core.autocrlf false operationally for the same
# reason; this rule is the in-repo half.
.claude/hooks/role_review_gate.py text eol=lf
.claude/hooks/write_attestation.py text eol=lf
.claude/agents/incident-analyst.md text eol=lf
.claude/tools/** text eol=lf

# The goldens are byte-exact fixtures: their bytes ARE the assertion.
# They are read with read_text, whose universal-newline translation
# hides a line-ending rewrite from the comparison, so a CRLF checkout
# passes for a reason unrelated to the emitter being right. Pinning
# them to LF makes the file on disk the same on every machine, which
# is what "byte-exact" has to mean before the phrase is worth writing.
# The whitespace pre-commit hooks are excluded from this directory for
# the same reason (.pre-commit-config.yaml), after one of them rewrote
# a golden's last byte on 2026-08-07.
tests/goldens/** text eol=lf
